In this situation your "freedom" would be illusory.  (This example
shows the distinction between my #1 definition "feeling of free will"
and #2 -- it satisfies #1 but not #2.)  Since the ability to reason is
a prerequisite for "free will" version #2, removal of reasoning powers
----> removal of free will.  The feeling of free will in picking the
fight is an illusion.  But this doesn't mean that our normal feeling
of free will is an illusion; just because drugs can give us a false
perception we needn't conclude that our perception is false when we're
sober. 
	       
