Since 'I' am my system, if my system causes something to happen then 
'I' have caused it to happen.  If I claim that my brain is under my
conscious control, you might say, "But you're also under the control of
your brain."  This seems to be like the person who describes a half-full
glass as half-empty -- why go for the pessimistic description when the
alternative is at least equally valid?  It's a partnership -- the brain
gets to control the involuntary functions, and the individual controls
voluntary movements, just so long as they aren't paralysed. 

In one description we're waves in reality space, constantly diverging
into the futures that we select.  Another description would have us all
as slaves.  (A very tenuous link in memespace with the song
